We examine the nonlinear Schr\"odinger equation within the exterior of a convex barrier, where the nonlinearity is of power type. We establish that the solution blows up in finite time for any initial data possessing sufficiently large energy and sufficiently large $L^2$ norm. Furthermore, we demonstrate that the blow-up rate is governed by the critical Sobolev exponent. Finally, we prove that the blow-up occurs at a single point. These findings extend the results previously obtained by Merle and Zaag for the entire space $\mathbb{R}^N$.
