This paper examines the logical systems developed by Kurt G\"odel, Alfred Tarski, Rudolf Carnap, and John Rosser, with a specific focus on the interplay between their work on the L\"ob theorem and the Tarski theorem. We demonstrate that the L\"ob theorem can be derived from the Tarski theorem, and conversely, that the Tarski theorem can be derived from the L\"ob theorem. Furthermore, we establish that the L\"ob theorem is equivalent to the Tarski theorem within the framework of the modal logic S4. Finally, we provide a proof of the L\"ob theorem that does not rely on the Tarski theorem.
